Subject: [PATCH 07860/11362] [outer-loop] exp5904: coordinate-blind live
 router PROVEN + repaired (default-off); gain over static salience
 UNESTABLISHED

DEFECT PROVEN, not argued: the shipped live router's within-state AUROC is EXACTLY 0.500 on a
click-dependent label -- a coordinate-blind scorer is mathematically a no-op, so click order was
decided entirely by the upstream static area x color-rarity salience sort. A test now loads the
REAL committed v3 checkpoint and asserts the one-distinct-score collapse, so a v3 change or a
default flip fails loudly.

REPAIR: new arc_click_target_features.py (664 lines, per-frame context + O(1)-ish per-candidate)
and an OnlineClickTargetRouter that fits WITHIN-EPISODE from the agent's own observed click
outcomes -- deliberately NOT cross-game (ops/exclusion_manifest.yaml
cross_game_value_transfer_retired_exp4342_v401 retires that direction; a hidden-game agent has
nothing to transfer from anyway). DEFAULT-OFF inside the router module; arc_competition_agent.py
untouched (owned by a concurrent workflow), so observe_click_outcome has NO live caller yet.

HONEST RESULT -- informativeness NOT established:
  within-state AUROC  blind 0.500 (exact) | coord 0.9797 | static_salience 0.9360
                      random 0.631 | step_index 0.500
  honest comparator   coord - static = +0.0436, bootstrap CI95 [-0.0302, +0.1245],
                      P(delta<=0) = 0.133, excludes_zero: FALSE
  random-arm noise floor sd 0.0717 = ~1.65x the headline delta
  HARD slice (level-ups | changed): coord 0.507 < static 0.660 < random 0.707 (n=20, 5 pos)
  label measured IDENTICAL to frame-change (182/182), so the 0.98 is carried by the trivial
  'does this click do anything' component that static salience already gets at 0.936
  informativeness_gate FAILS; gate_of_record; informativeness_established: false
  1 game (lp85), 182 rows, 4 states -- a smoke, far under the N>=30 level-up floor

The review also DELETED a misleading 'pre_registered_gate: passed true' (a capstone would have
read it as a win) and replaced it with coordinate_blindness_repair_check carrying a MEASURED
also_passed_by_arms: ['random','static_salience'] -- i.e. the original gate was passable by
random. Offline AUROC licenses nothing (exp4545 regressed live search); terminal gate is a live
banked-levels A/B, stratified on frame_diff_ground_truth_validated.

Verified: 79 tests pass (0 skips); arc_orphan_solver_lint OK (62 modules in live closure);
adversarial_verify 0 flagged; ruff/format/canonical-url/verifier-authenticity clean; ZERO new
test failures vs a clean git-worktree HEAD baseline (comm diff of failure sets).

